From 9422629e5df4eeaac79d0e02f4972e415ee37291 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Schaff <schaff.jim@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:20:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Build fixes for OPTION_VCELL with modern toolchains and the
 Python module

OPTION_VCELL (the VCell hybrid hooks: ValueProvider, AbstractMesh,
smoldynhybrid.c) no longer compiled upstream. Fixes, all no-ops for the
default OPTION_VCELL=OFF build:

- CMake: compile Smoldyn sources (and libSteve's SimCommand.c) as C++
  under OPTION_VCELL, since smoldyn.h declares C++ classes in that mode
  (as VCell's vendored Smoldyn does); repeat for source/python's copy.
- CMake: default BNG2_PATH before the platform branches (the VCELL
  branch skipped it).
- CMake: link the system zlib; drop the Windows-era zlib.h/zconf.h
  from source/vcell, which shadowed it and no longer compile.
- libSteve: extern "C" guards on headers that lacked them, so C++
  callers link against the C-compiled library.
- smolcomparts.c: fix extern "C" { #include "zlib.h" } whose closing
  brace was swallowed by the include line.
- smolsurface.c: pass the index argument added to surfsetrate().
- smolfilament.c: cast calloc results for C++.
- smoldyn.h: include <sstream> for the VCell rate parsing.
- python/module.cpp: include SimpleMesh.h / SimpleValueProvider.h.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
